hadiths[25]{hadithnumber,text}:
"537","Abdullah narrated to us: Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to me: Hushaym narrated to us who said: Abu al-Miqdam claimed from al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan who said: I entered the mosque, and there was Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, reclining upon his cloak, then two water-carriers came disputing to him, so he judged between them. Then I came to him and looked at him, and he was a handsome-faced man with smallpox marks on his cheek, and his hair had covered his forearms."
"538","Waki narrated to us: Umm Ghurab narrated to me from Bunanah who said: Uthman never dyed at all."
"539","Abdullah narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me: Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us: Waqid ibn Abdullah al-Tamimi narrated to me from one who saw Uthman ibn Affan capping his teeth with gold."
"540","Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us from dictation who said: Muhammad ibn Qays al-Asadi informed us from Musa ibn Talhah who said: I heard Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, while upon the pulpit with the caller establishing prayer, while he was asking the people, questioning them about their news and their prices."
"541","Abdullah narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Said narrated to me: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us from Ibn Shihab from al-Saib ibn Yazid that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, prostrated in Sad."
"542","Abdullah narrated to us: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me: Mahbub ibn Muhriz, seller of glass, Kufan, trustworthy - thus Surayj said - narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah, meaning Ibn Farrukh, from his father who said: I prayed behind Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, the Eid, so he said takbir seven and five."
"543","Abdussamad narrated to us: Salim Abu Jumay narrated to us: Al-Hasan narrated to us, and he mentioned Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, and the intensity of his shyness, and said: He would be in the house with the door closed upon him, yet he would not remove the garment to pour water over himself, shyness preventing him from straightening his back."
"544","Ibrahim ibn Khalid al-Sanani narrated to us: Umayyah ibn Shibl and others narrated to me, they said: Uthman ruled twelve years, and the tribulation was five years."
"545","Ishaq ibn Isa ibn al-Tabba narrated to us from Abu Mashar who said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed on Friday with eighteen days passed of Dhu al-Hijjah in the year thirty-five, and his caliphate was twelve years except twelve days."
"546","Abdullah narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated to me: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us who said: My father said: Abu Uthman narrated to us that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed in the middle of the days of Tashriq."
"547","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Abu Hilal narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us that Uthman was killed while he was ninety years old or eighty-eight."
"548","Abdullah narrated to us: Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to me: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Abu Khaldah narrated to us from Abu al-Aliyah who said: We were at the door of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, in the ten of Adha."
"549","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us from Qatadah who said: Al-Zubayr prayed over Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, and buried him, and he had bequeathed to him."
"550","Zakariya ibn Adi narrated to us from Ubaydullah ibn Amr from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil who said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed in the year thirty-five, so the tribulation was five years, of them four months for al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him."
"551","Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Abu Khaldah narrated to us from Abu al-Aliyah who said: We were at the door of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, in the ten of Adha."
"552","Abdullah narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me: Al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aws al-Ansari narrated to me: Abu Ubadah al-Zuraqi al-Ansari of the people of Madinah narrated to me from Zayd ibn Aslam from his father who said: I witnessed Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, on the day he was besieged in the place of funerals, and if a stone were cast it would fall only upon the head of a man. So I saw Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, looking out from the small door which is toward the station of Jibril, peace be upon him, and he said: O people, is Talhah among you? They were silent. Then he said: O people, is Talhah among you? They were silent. Then he said: O people, is Talhah among you? So Talhah ibn Ubaydullah stood and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: Do I not see you here? I did not think you would be in a group hearing my call the last of three times then not answering me. I adjure you by Allah, O Talhah, do you remember the day when I and you were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in such-and-such place, with none of his companions with him other than me and you? He said: Yes. He said to you, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Talhah, there is no prophet except with him from his companions is a companion from his nation with him in Paradise, and Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, this - meaning me - is my companion with me in Paradise. Talhah said: O Allah, yes. Then he left."
"553","Abdullah narrated to us: Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to me: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us: Said narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us from Muslim ibn Yasar from Humran ibn Aban that he witnessed Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, performing ablution one day: He rinsed and sniffed and washed his face three times, and narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to the hadith of Ibn Jafar from Said."
"554","Abdullah narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to me: Khalid, meaning Ibn Abdullah, informed us from al-Jurayri from Urwah ibn Qabisah from a man of the Ansar from his father who said: I was standing with Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: Shall I not inform you how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution? We said: Yes indeed. So he called for water and washed his face three times and rinsed and sniffed three times, then washed his hands to his elbows three times, then wiped his head and his ears, and washed his feet three times, then said: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution."
"555","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us: Hilal ibn Hiqq narrated to us from al-Jurayri from Thumamah ibn Hazn al-Qushayri who said: I witnessed the House on the day Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, was struck. He looked out upon them a look and said: Call for me your two companions who incited you against me. So they were called for him, and he said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah the mosque became straitened for its people, so he said: Whoever buys this plot from his pure wealth, so he is in it as the Muslims, and for him is better than it in Paradise? So I bought it from my pure wealth and made it for the Muslims, while you prevent me from praying in it two rakahs. Then he said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah there was no well from which sweet water was taken except Rumah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys it from his pure wealth, so his bucket in it is as the buckets of the Muslims, and for him is better than it in Paradise? So I bought it from my pure wealth, while you prevent me from drinking from it. Then he said: Do you know that I am the equipper of the Army of Hardship? They said: O Allah, yes."
"556","Abdullah narrated to us: My father and Abu Khaythamah narrated to me, they said: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Zaidah narrated to us from Asim from Shaqiq who said: Abdurrahman ibn Awf met al-Walid ibn Uqbah, so al-Walid said to him: Why do I see you have shunned the Commander of the Believers Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him? Abdurrahman said: Convey to him. Then he mentioned the hadith. As for his saying that I stayed back on the day of Badr, for I was nursing Ruqayyah daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until she died, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck for me a share, and whoever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) strikes for a share has indeed witnessed. Then he mentioned the hadith in full to its end."
"557","Abdullah narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to me: Qabisah narrated to me from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash from Asim from Abu Wail who said: I said to Abdurrahman ibn Awf: How did you pledge to Uthman and leave Ali, may Allah be pleased with him? He said: What is my fault? I began with Ali and said: I pledge you upon the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger and the conduct of Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. He said: So he said: In what I am able. He said: Then I offered it to Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, so he accepted it."
"558","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Layth narrated to us: Zuhrah ibn Mabad al-Qurashi narrated to us from Abu Salih, freedman of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard Uthman saying upon the pulpit: O people, I concealed from you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) out of dislike that you disperse from me, then it occurred to me to narrate it to you so a man may choose for himself what appears to him. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Guarding a day in the path of Allah is better than a thousand days in other dwellings."
"559","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim Bahili narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abdurrahman ibn Abi Dhubab narrated to us, and he mentioned it."
"560","Abu Said narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Musa ibn Wardan informed us who said: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyab saying: I heard Uthman addressing upon the pulpit, saying: I used to buy dates from a clan of the Jews called Banu Qaynuqa, then sell them for profit by the sa. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O Uthman, when you buy, then take by measure, and when you sell, then give by measure."
"561","Bishr ibn Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us: My father narrated to me from al-Zuhri: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me that Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar informed him that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Allah sent Muhammad with the truth, blessings and peace be upon him, so I was among those who answered Allah and His Messenger and believed in what Muhammad was sent with, blessings and peace be upon him. Then I emigrated the two emigrations and attained marriage relation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). By Allah, I neither disobeyed him nor deceived him until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, took him."
